### Bookstore API - smoke tests (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client)
### Start the stack first: docker compose up -d --build
### Each request is annotated with the response observed against the current implementation.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api

### Health check -> 200, empty body
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/health

### List all books -> 200, JSON array
GET {{baseUrl}}/books

### List books of a category (exact, case-sensitive name) -> 200, filtered array
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?category=Programming

### Unknown category -> 200, ALL books (no filtering applied)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?category=programming

### Create a book -> 201, Book with integer categoryId
# @name createBook
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test Driven Development",
  "author": "Kent Beck",
  "categoryId": "Programming",
  "quantity": 3,
  "description": "A book about TDD",
  "language": "English",
  "active": true,
  "publisher": "Addison-Wesley",
  "publisherDate": "2002-11-08T00:00:00Z"
}

### Create without title -> 404, empty body
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "author": "Nobody" }

### Create with unknown category name -> 500 (HTML error page)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Bad Category", "categoryId": "Poetry" }

### Create with malformed JSON -> 500 (HTML error page, not 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": 

### Create with an empty body -> 400, empty body
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

### Create with a date without offset -> 500
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Date only", "publisherDate": "2002-11-08" }

### Create with wrong content type -> 415
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: text/plain

hello

### Get one book by exact title -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/single?name=Test%20Driven%20Development

### Get one book by id -> 200 with EMPTY body (id lookup never matches, see known issues)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/single?id={{createBook.response.body.id}}

### Get one book with unknown title -> 200 with EMPTY body
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/single?name=Unknown

### Get one book by author -> 500 (not implemented)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/single?author=Kent%20Beck

### Update stock and keep the book active -> 201, partial Book
PUT {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "{{createBook.response.body.id}}", "quantity": 10, "active": true }

### Update stock WITHOUT "active" -> 201, book is DEACTIVATED and inactiveDate is set
PUT {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "{{createBook.response.body.id}}", "quantity": 5 }

### Update without id -> 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 5, "active": true }

### Update with an unknown id -> 201, nothing changes
PUT {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "000000000000000000000000", "quantity": 5, "active": true }

### Update with malformed id -> 500
PUT {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "not-an-object-id", "quantity": 5, "active": true }

### Unsupported method -> 405
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/books

### Unacceptable Accept header -> 406
GET {{baseUrl}}/books
Accept: application/xml

### OpenAPI document -> 200 application/yaml
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi.yaml

### Swagger UI -> 200 text/html (open in a browser)
GET {{baseUrl}}/docs
